{"id":2902,"age":11,"sex":"F","race":"Non-Hispanic White","insurance":"Private Commercial Insurance","profile":{"sex":"F","allergies":["NKDA"],"insurance":"Private Commercial Insurance","occupation":"Student (6th grade)","alcohol_use":"None","family_history":["Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal cousin","Autoimmune thyroiditis (Hashimoto disease) in mother","Celiac disease in maternal aunt"],"race_ethnicity":"Non-Hispanic White","smoking_status":"Never","home_medications":[{"dose":"Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily (morning and bedtime)","name":"Insulin NPH (intermediate-acting)"},{"dose":"Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily with breakfast and dinner per carbohydrate ratio and sliding scale","name":"Insulin Regular (short-acting)"}],"surgical_history":["Tympanostomy tube placement (age 4)"],"chronic_conditions":["Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed age 3)"],"age_at_first_encounter":11},"comorbidities_listed":["Dehydration","Type 1 diabetes mellitus","Upper respiratory tract infection","Hypovolemia"],"primary":{"did":527,"code":"E10.10","name":"Diabetic ketoacidosis"},"filing":{"chapter":4,"block":"E08-E13","block_desc":"Diabetes mellitus (E08-E13)"},"encounters":[{"id":12309,"date":"2020-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Maria Rodriguez","cc":"Extreme tiredness and appearing \"out of it\" since this morning, with one week of polyuria and polydipsia following a resolved upper respiratory infection.","order":0,"method":"template","question_ids":[6758],"sections":[{"sid":59738,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Extreme tiredness and appearing \"out of it\" since this morning, with one week of polyuria and polydipsia following a resolved upper respiratory infection."]},{"sid":59739,"type":"hpi","lines":["Over the past week, she has been getting up multiple times at night to urinate and has been asking for more water than usual during the day.","Her mother also notes that she recently had a sore throat and runny nose, which resolved without treatment 5 days ago.","This morning, the girl complained of abdominal pain and appeared confused and slow to respond to questions.","She has not eaten since last night and vomited once this morning."]},{"sid":59740,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed age 3)"]},{"sid":59741,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tympanostomy tube placement (age 4)"]},{"sid":59742,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Insulin NPH (intermediate-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily (morning and bedtime)","- Insulin Regular (short-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily with breakfast and dinner per carbohydrate ratio and sliding scale"]},{"sid":59743,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":59744,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal cousin","- Autoimmune thyroiditis (Hashimoto disease) in mother","- Celiac disease in maternal aunt"]},{"sid":59745,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Student (6th grade)."]},{"sid":59746,"type":"vitals","lines":["She is tachypneic. Her blood pressure is mildly low and pulse is elevated."]},{"sid":59747,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, she appears dehydrated with dry mucous membranes and sunken eyes.","Her breathing is deep and rapid.","Capillary refill is delayed.","She is oriented only to person.","Cardiac and lung examinations are otherwise normal.","There are no signs of trauma, rash, or focal neurologic deficits."]},{"sid":59748,"type":"labs","lines":["A urine dipstick reveals the presence of ketones and glucose.","Arterial blood gas is obtained, and serum chemistries are pending."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":12311,"date":"2021-04-15","type":"inpatient","dept":"Pediatrics","attending":"Dr. Sarah Chen","cc":"Confusion and vomiting after polydipsia and polyuria while staying with aunt for the weekend.","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5035],"sections":[{"sid":59749,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Confusion and vomiting after polydipsia and polyuria while staying with aunt for the weekend."]},{"sid":59750,"type":"hpi","lines":["This 12-year-old female with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus diagnosed at age 3 years and a prior diabetic ketoacidosis admission in January 2020 presents with recurrent symptoms.","The aunt reports the patient had been staying with her for the weekend and has seemed \u201coff\u201d since yesterday.","She notes the child has been drinking large amounts of water and frequently asking to use the bathroom, including overnight.","This morning, the girl vomited twice and was found sitting on the bathroom floor breathing rapidly and muttering incoherently."]},{"sid":59751,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Diabetic ketoacidosis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed age 3)","","She has a history of a chronic medical condition."]},{"sid":59752,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tympanostomy tube placement (age 4)"]},{"sid":59753,"type":"medications","lines":["Is.","","Home Medications:","- Insulin NPH (intermediate-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily (morning and bedtime)","- Insulin Regular (short-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily with breakfast and dinner per carbohydrate ratio and sliding scale"]},{"sid":59754,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":59755,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal cousin","- Autoimmune thyroiditis (Hashimoto disease) in mother","- Celiac disease in maternal aunt"]},{"sid":59756,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Student (6th grade)."]},{"sid":59757,"type":"vitals","lines":["Her blood pressure is 86/54 mm Hg and heart rate is 124/min. Respiratory rate is 30/min"]},{"sid":59758,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Upon arrival, the patient is drowsy, tachypneic, and has dry mucous membranes and cool extremities. her breathing is deep and labored.","A fruity odor is noted on her breath.","She is oriented only to person and is slow to respond.","She does not localize pain but withdraws to it.","Pupils are reactive and no focal neurologic deficits are noted.","Cardiac and pulmonary exams are unremarkable."]},{"sid":59759,"type":"labs","lines":["Fingerstick glucose reads \u201cHI\u201d on the monitor.","Urinalysis is positive for glucose and ketones.","Initial labs confirm a high anion gap metabolic acidosis."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":12310,"date":"2022-04-15","type":"inpatient","dept":"Pediatrics","attending":"Dr. James Park","cc":"Severe lethargy and confusion after potentially forgetting evening insulin dose during a sleepover at a friend's house.","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4208],"sections":[{"sid":59760,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Severe lethargy and confusion after potentially forgetting evening insulin dose during a sleepover at a friend's house."]},{"sid":59761,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 13-year-old female with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus who presents with severe lethargy and confusion, similar to her prior admissions in January 2020 and April 2021 when she experienced extreme tiredness and confusion following polyuria and polydipsia.","The parents report that the child had been invited to a sleepover at a friend's house the night before.","She has had type 1 diabetes mellitus for 3 years and typically uses a basal-bolus insulin regimen, but they believe she may have forgotten to bring or take her evening insulin dose.","This morning, the friend's mother called to say the girl had been difficult to wake and was acting \"strangely,\" speaking incoherently and seeming disoriented.","When the parents arrived, she was weak, breathing heavily, and unable to answer questions appropriately.","She recently recovered from a mild viral upper respiratory illness without complications.","She had not eaten since dinner the night before but had consumed large amounts of soda and candy at the sleepover."]},{"sid":59762,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Diabetic ketoacidosis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed age 3)","","Her past medical history is otherwise unremarkable."]},{"sid":59763,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tympanostomy tube placement (age 4)"]},{"sid":59764,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes no other medications.","","Home Medications:","- Insulin NPH (intermediate-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily (morning and bedtime)","- Insulin Regular (short-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily with breakfast and dinner per carbohydrate ratio and sliding scale"]},{"sid":59765,"type":"allergies","lines":["She has no known drug allergies"]},{"sid":59766,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal cousin","- Autoimmune thyroiditis (Hashimoto disease) in mother","- Celiac disease in maternal aunt"]},{"sid":59767,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Student (6th grade)."]},{"sid":59768,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, she is tachycardic and tachypneic, with dry mucous membranes, deep labored breathing, and a fruity odor to her breath.","She is oriented only to self and appears severely dehydrated.","Her capillary refill is delayed and her skin is cool to the touch.","Cardiac and pulmonary exams are otherwise normal."]},{"sid":59769,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory tests are ordered and confirm the suspected diagnosis."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":12308,"date":"2023-04-15","type":"icu","dept":"Pediatric Critical Care","attending":"Dr. Aisha Johnson","cc":"Progressive abdominal discomfort, nausea, repeated vomiting, and altered mental status after missing insulin doses due to poor oral intake.","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4162],"sections":[{"sid":59770,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive abdominal discomfort, nausea, repeated vomiting, and altered mental status after missing insulin doses due to poor oral intake."]},{"sid":59771,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 14-year-old female with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus diagnosed at age 3, returning with recurrent symptoms similar to her prior diabetic ketoacidosis presentations in 2020, 2021, and 2022.","She is brought to the hospital with a 6-hour history of progressive abdominal discomfort, nausea, and repeated vomiting.","Her mother reports that the patient has been fatigued and less responsive but can be awakened to voice.","The patient has not received any insulin today due to concerns about eating poorly."]},{"sid":59772,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Diabetic ketoacidosis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed age 3)","","She was diagnosed with type 1 diabetes mellitus at age 3."]},{"sid":59773,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tympanostomy tube placement (age 4)"]},{"sid":59774,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes currently uses a basal-bolus insulin regimen with intermediate and short-acting insulin administered twice daily.","","Home Medications:","- Insulin NPH (intermediate-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily (morning and bedtime)","- Insulin Regular (short-acting) Variable units administered subcutaneously twice daily with breakfast and dinner per carbohydrate ratio and sliding scale"]},{"sid":59775,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":59776,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal cousin","- Autoimmune thyroiditis (Hashimoto disease) in mother","- Celiac disease in maternal aunt"]},{"sid":59777,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: None. Occupation: Student (6th grade)."]},{"sid":59778,"type":"vitals","lines":["Her vital signs show a mildly decreased blood pressure, a heart rate of 98/min, and deep, rapid breathing at 22/min"]},{"sid":59779,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Examination reveals tachypnea with deep respirations, fruity-smelling breath, and mild dehydration"]},{"sid":59780,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory analysis demonstrates severe hyperglycemia, markedly reduced serum bicarbonate, and a potassium level at the upper end of normal"]}],"orders":[]}],"problems":[{"did":527,"code":"E10.10","name":"Diabetic ketoacidosis","icd_desc":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis without coma","snomed":"420422005","snomed_desc":"Ketoacidosis due to diabetes mellitus","category":"Endocrine","acuity":"acute","kind":"active","first_enc":12309,"chapter":4,"block":"E08-E13","docs":[{"enc":12309,"how":"encounter diagnosis"},{"enc":12311,"how":"encounter diagnosis"},{"enc":12310,"how":"encounter diagnosis"},{"enc":12308,"how":"problem list mention"}],"primary":true},{"did":4838,"code":"E10.11","name":"Diabetic ketoacidosis","icd_desc":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis with coma","snomed":"420422005","snomed_desc":"Ketoacidosis due to diabetes mellitus","category":"Endocrine","acuity":"acute_on_chronic","kind":"chronic","first_enc":12308,"chapter":4,"block":"E08-E13","docs":[{"enc":12308,"how":"encounter diagnosis"}],"primary":false},{"did":2790,"code":"E10.9","name":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus","icd_desc":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus without complications","snomed":"46635009","snomed_desc":"Diabetes mellitus type 1","category":"Endocrine","acuity":"chronic","kind":"secondary","first_enc":12309,"chapter":4,"block":"E08-E13","docs":[{"enc":12309,"how":"secondary diagnosis"},{"enc":12311,"how":"secondary diagnosis"},{"enc":12310,"how":"secondary diagnosis"},{"enc":12308,"how":"secondary diagnosis"}],"primary":false},{"did":1772,"code":"J06.9","name":"Upper respiratory tract infection","icd_desc":"Acute upper respiratory infection, unspecified","snomed":"54150009","snomed_desc":"Upper respiratory infection","category":"Infectious","acuity":"acute","kind":"secondary","first_enc":12309,"chapter":10,"block":"J00-J06","docs":[{"enc"